# DM26-0670
# infra/load-plans/pressure.nuon
#
# The broker's budget past its growth threshold (docs/architecture/broker-baseline.md, the fifth set, (b)): its
# controller grows the budget only while it holds three quarters of it, and one publisher and one held-back subscriber
# hold about three eighths (a connection's window is a quarter of the budget, a subscriber's high water an eighth), so
# reaching three quarters needs about three publishers held back at once. harness-producer is multi-instance
# (docs/architecture/authority-model.md, "Multi-instance workloads"), so 3 and 6 producers run as 3 and 6 sessions, each
# at 1,000 messages a second, against one sink spending its delay before it acknowledges each delivery
# (`sink_slow: "before_ack"`): 1.1 ms (about a quarter of three producers' rate) or 10 ms, at 64 KiB and 1 MiB. Ten
# seconds of messages a producer, at most 1 GiB each. The broker restarted before every run (`fresh_broker`), so each
# begins at its floor; acceptance: `budget_max` above the floor (268,435,456) and `limited_by` past `Floor`, nothing
# lost, the peak within the container's limit. The producer waits 120 s for an acknowledgement and the sink 60 s for a
# message. 8 runs.
#
#   nu infra/load-harness.nu run infra/load-plans/pressure.nuon --target sandbox-local
{
  name: "pressure"
  fresh_broker: true
  defaults: {
    rate: 1000, seconds: 10, max_count: 10000, max_bytes: 1073741824, warmup: 100,
    sink_slow: "before_ack", stall_secs: 120, idle_secs: 60
  }
  grid: {
    size: [65536 1048576]
    sink_delay_us: [1100 10000]
    shape: [
      { producers: 3, sinks: 1, lanes: 1 }
      { producers: 6, sinks: 1, lanes: 1 }
    ]
  }
}
